{
  // Scoped typecheck project for this package's `test/` tree. `check-types`
  // runs it as a SECOND `tsc` pass (after the composite `tsc -b`), because the
  // composite build emits declarations only for `src` and never sees `test/**`.
  // We re-include `src` so producer module augmentations (e.g. triage's
  // `declare module "../agent/decision-traces"`) are guaranteed active in the
  // program, then add `test` on top.
  //
  // The base `tsconfig.json` is `composite: true`; a `tsc -p` invocation with
  // `noEmit` errors unless `composite`/`declaration` are overridden off here.
  // Nothing under `test` is emitted or built — this project only type-checks.
  //
  // `rootDir: "."` is also the fence: a test that reaches into another package
  // by a relative path (`../../../assistant/src/...`) is TS6059/TS6307 here and
  // is caught by nothing else in the repo.
  //
  // `exclude` is a BASELINE, not a policy. Every path below is a file that
  // carried at least one diagnostic when this tree first entered the program,
  // and each is a debt to be repaid rather than a file that is allowed to be
  // unchecked. `pnpm check:test-typecheck-baseline` derives this list from `tsc`
  // and fails when it drifts in either direction: an entry whose file is now
  // clean or absent must be deleted, and a file that is dirty and unlisted must
  // be repaired. Paths are literal on purpose — a directory glob such as
  // `"test/dispatch"` would silently un-check every file added tomorrow.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"],
  "exclude": [
    "test/agent/chat-context-assembly.test.ts",
    "test/agent/chat-turn-closure-artifact-strand.test.ts",
    "test/agent/commit-cancel-race.test.ts",
    "test/agent/conversation-compaction-wait.test.ts",
